{
  "tag": "md-status-dot",
  "className": "MdStatusDot",
  "properties": [
    {
      "name": "state",
      "type": "MdStatusDotState",
      "default": "'neutral'",
      "defaultValue": "neutral",
      "options": [],
      "mutable": false,
      "reflect": true,
      "attribute": "state",
      "optional": false,
      "description": "Presence state. Drives the dot's fill color and its corresponding\npulse-halo color (when `live` is `true`)."
    },
    {
      "name": "size",
      "type": "MdStatusDotSize",
      "default": "'medium'",
      "defaultValue": "medium",
      "options": [],
      "mutable": false,
      "reflect": true,
      "attribute": "size",
      "optional": false,
      "description": "Diameter preset:\n- `small`  — 8 px (pairs with `md-avatar size=\"small\"`)\n- `medium` — 12 px (pairs with `md-avatar size=\"medium\"` — default)\n- `large`  — 16 px (pairs with `md-avatar size=\"large\"`)\n\nCustom diameters are exposed via the `--md-status-dot-size` CSS\ncustom property on the host."
    },
    {
      "name": "inline",
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": "false",
      "defaultValue": false,
      "options": [],
      "mutable": false,
      "reflect": true,
      "attribute": "inline",
      "optional": false,
      "description": "Lay the dot out in normal flow instead of as an absolutely-positioned\ncorner badge.\n\nThe default mode is the avatar badge: `position: absolute` pinned 2px\noutside its positioned parent's inline/block end, with a surface-toned\nhalo separating it from the tile beneath. That is wrong wherever the dot\nsits BESIDE something — a legend swatch, a \"Market open\" line, a status\nlabel in a table cell — where it needs to flow with the text. Without\nthis prop each such use had to wrap the dot in a `position: relative`\nspan of an explicit size AND null out both inset custom properties; miss\none and the dot hangs low and to the right, overlapping its own label.\n\n`inline` makes the host an `inline-block` in normal flow, vertically\ncentred on the text, with no halo (the halo exists to separate the dot\nfrom an avatar tile; over ordinary text it reads as a stray ring). Set\n`--md-status-dot-outline-width` to bring it back."
    },
    {
      "name": "shape",
      "type": "'rect' | 'circle'",
      "default": "'rect'",
      "defaultValue": "rect",
      "options": [
        "rect",
        "circle"
      ],
      "mutable": false,
      "reflect": true,
      "attribute": "shape",
      "optional": false,
      "description": "The SHAPE of the thing the dot is anchored to.\n\nThe dot anchors to the bottom-inline-end corner of its containing block,\nwhich is right for a `rect` host — a tile, a table cell, a rounded avatar\nsquare. It is wrong for a `circle`, because a circle's bounding-box corner\nlies outside the visible shape: measured on a 40px round avatar, the\ndefault anchor left the dot's centre 5.5px clear of the rim, floating in\nthe gap with nothing behind it.\n\n`circle` puts the dot ON the rim, at the 45° point where a presence dot\nbelongs. The maths is percentage-based, so it holds at every avatar size\nwithout the dot having to be told what that size is: the rim at 45° sits\n`(1 − 1/√2) / 2 ≈ 14.6447%` of the diameter in from each edge, and half the\ndot's own size comes back off to centre it there.\n\n`rect` stays the default deliberately — it is what a dot on a tile, a card\nor a table cell wants, and changing the default would move every dot that\nalready exists."
    },
    {
      "name": "live",
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": "false",
      "defaultValue": false,
      "options": [],
      "mutable": false,
      "reflect": true,
      "attribute": "live",
      "optional": false,
      "description": "Pulse the dot outward in its own colour. Useful for \"live now\",\n\"in a call\", \"recording\" affordances. Respects\n`prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` automatically."
    },
    {
      "name": "label",
      "type": "string",
      "default": "''",
      "defaultValue": "",
      "options": [],
      "mutable": false,
      "reflect": false,
      "attribute": "label",
      "optional": false,
      "description": "Optional accessible label.\n\n- When **empty** (default), the dot is exposed to AT as decorative\n  (`role=\"presentation\"` + `aria-hidden=\"true\"`) so the parent\n  element (typically an `md-avatar` or a list-item) can carry the\n  spoken status without doubling.\n- When **set** and `live` is **off**, the dot becomes `role=\"img\"` with\n  the value as its `aria-label` — a static, labelled status image.\n- When **set** and `live` is **on**, the dot becomes a `role=\"status\"`\n  live region so presence *changes* are announced as they occur. Use this\n  for standalone dots that aren't paired with another labelled element."
    },
    {
      "name": "density",
      "type": "0 | -1 | -2 | -3 | -4",
      "default": "0",
      "defaultValue": 0,
      "options": [],
      "mutable": false,
      "reflect": true,
      "attribute": "density",
      "optional": false,
      "description": "Local density rung. Drives the same `--md-sys-density-scale` signal that a\nglobal `data-density` ancestor sets, so a local value simply overrides the\ninherited one. 0 = default, -4 = ultra-compact."
    }
  ],
  "state": [],
  "events": [],
  "methods": [],
  "slots": [],
  "cssParts": [],
  "cssProperties": [
